{
  "body": "Independent M4 Code Review covers ab6225a4..0f7bc0ca against the approved primary plan and reconciled Design package. The scope includes public v3 creation, explicit existing-v2 continuation, version-aware validators and selectors, package contents, historical fixture isolation, canonical consumer guidance and governance adoption. The two selector files were corrected by the author after exact-subject inspection; this assessment retains their submitted commit identities and does not assess the unreviewed correction.\n\nPublic creation policy is enforced in primary and advanced adapters while existing v2 stores and their recovery remain supported. Test-only historical initialization preserves real public continuation and recovery assertions. Package inventory and consumer guidance account for separate stored/request/result version domains, meaningful explanation fields, partial-read omissions, explicit applicability and success-only Verify. The scoped user decision v3-finding-id-only and current Design carry the revised direction; the original proposal approval remains explicitly stale and is not treated as approval of that revision. The reviewed Design clarification leaves the Delivery allocation applicable.\n\nIndependent execution of node --test packages/rigorloop/test/record-store-v3-adoption.test.js packages/rigorloop/test/record-store-v2-persistence.test.js passed 54 cases. Inspection of m4-implementation evidence establishes the reported 432 npm tests, 256 record-store tests, selector/metadata/package/skill checks and all 21 selected PR-mode checks against the submitted candidate. These passing suites do not cover collection-valued manifest discriminators: an independent temporary-store select_validation reproduction with schema_version:[] raises TypeError rather than returning the explicit blocked result. A bounded implementation correction and regression are required at that input boundary.\n\nThis is milestone assessment only. It supplies neither final whole-change Code Review nor Verify, hosted CI, publication or merge evidence.",
  "change_id": "2026-09-10-structured-assessment-explanations",
  "contributors": [
    {
      "id": "codex-implement",
      "role": "implement"
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "Severity: major\nLocation: scripts/validation_selection.py:1020, manifest contract discriminator dispatch.\nThe supported-pair set membership hashes untrusted JSON schema_version and contract values. A temporary docs/changes/example/change.json containing schema_version:[] and contract:\"rigorloop-records-v3\", passed to select_validation(SelectionRequest(mode=\"explicit\", paths=(\"docs/changes/example/change.json\",), repo_root=root)), independently raises TypeError: unhashable type: list. Object-valued discriminators have the same source-level defect. This escapes the structured unsupported-change-contract blocker and prevents normal selection/diagnostics for malformed current manifests. Scalar unknown-version tests do not cover this new failure mode.",
      "id": "code-review-m4-f1",
      "origin": {
        "evidence": "Severity: major\nLocation: scripts/validation_selection.py:1020, manifest contract discriminator dispatch.\nThe supported-pair set membership hashes untrusted JSON schema_version and contract values. A temporary docs/changes/example/change.json containing schema_version:[] and contract:\"rigorloop-records-v3\", passed to select_validation(SelectionRequest(mode=\"explicit\", paths=(\"docs/changes/example/change.json\",), repo_root=root)), independently raises TypeError: unhashable type: list. Object-valued discriminators have the same source-level defect. This escapes the structured unsupported-change-contract blocker and prevents normal selection/diagnostics for malformed current manifests. Scalar unknown-version tests do not cover this new failure mode.",
        "rationale": "The selector owns explicit fail-closed classification of unsupported current manifests; arbitrary JSON discriminator types must not crash classification.",
        "reporter": {
          "id": "codex-code-review",
          "role": "review"
        },
        "required_outcome": "Reject array/object and other unsupported discriminator values through the explicit blocked selector result without an uncaught exception or legacy fallback. Use type-safe comparison and add malformed/unknown-value regressions for both schema_version and contract, preserving valid v2/v3 selection and existing unknown scalar behavior. Safe correction belongs to M4 implementation followed by independent rereview; no Design decision is required.",
        "subjects": [
          {
            "identity": "sha256:47cfb0fbe5afe9beade6961560cb69144b639588d01375e16341aa4fe2bcf7b2",
            "path": "scripts/test-select-validation.py"
          },
          {
            "identity": "sha256:18361bacee33608af13258090c9f0fb26e542d83ef5f569c3d5b9c834179e3b7",
            "path": "scripts/validation_selection.py"
          }
        ],
        "supporting_judgment": {
          "contributors": [
            {
              "id": "codex-implement",
              "role": "implement"
            }
          ],
          "independence_basis": "Separately delegated reviewer authored none of the M4 implementation, tests or canonical guidance; inspected the submitted exact diff and independently exercised relevant public boundaries. Parent /root authored the implementation.",
          "judgment": "changes-requested",
          "rationale": "Independent M4 assessment reproduced the malformed-input exception despite passing planned candidate checks.",
